# Endospore system_ext PUBLIC policy (NWP-20261116-37), wired by inject-product.sh as
# SYSTEM_EXT_PUBLIC_SEPOLICY_DIRS += vendor/endospore/sepolicy_public on every device.
#
# ONE attribute and nothing else. The DRM store (/data/vendor/mediadrm) is labelled mediadrm_vendor_data_file, and
# that type is NOT a platform type: each Pixel declares it in its own generated vendor policy
# (vendor/google_devices/<device>/sepolicy/vendor/types.te). Our private policy (vendor/endospore/sepolicy, the
# system_ext PRIVATE dir) compiles without the vendor policy in view, so naming the type there fails the build with
# "unknown type mediadrm_vendor_data_file" -- the 0.5.58 break NWP-20261203-08 shipped to main.
# The vendor policy, in turn, compiles against the PUBLIC policies only, so it can join a public attribute but can
# never name endospore_priv, which stays private. This attribute is the meeting point:
#   - vendor/endospore/sepolicy_vendor puts mediadrm_vendor_data_file into it, on a device whose vendor policy
#     declares that type;
#   - vendor/endospore/sepolicy/endospore.te grants endospore_priv delete-only access to it.
# On a device that does not join it, the attribute holds no type and the grant reaches nothing.
# Same pattern the Pixel trees use themselves: their system_ext public types.te declares hal_face_debug_* attributes
# that their vendor policy fills.
# NOTE: no backtick and no apostrophe in these comments -- the build runs .te through m4.
attribute nowhere_drm_store_file;
